text:
To create a colorful website using HTML and JS, we can start by creating a basic HTML structure, which includes a head, body, and title element. We can also add a CSS file to style the website and give it some colors.

Next, we can use JavaScript to replace the jokes with two real jokes, which can be stored in a separate JSON or text file.

HTML:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="joke-container">
      <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
      <div id="jokes"></div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
```
CSS:
```css
#jokes {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: row;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  margin: 10px 0;
}

.joke {
  margin: 5px;
}
```
JavaScript:
```javascript
// Load jokes from JSON/text file
const jokes = [];
jokes = JSON.parse(jokes);

// Replace jokes in the DOM
const jokeContainer = document.querySelector('#joke-container');
jokes.forEach(joke => {
  const jokeElement = document.createElement('div');
  jokeElement.classList.add('joke');
  jokeElement.innerText = joke;
  jokeContainer.appendChild(jokeElement);
});
```
This is a basic setup that can be expanded upon to create a fully functional and colorful joke website.

To turn this mock-up into a colorful and interactive website, you'll need to use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Here is an example of what the code could look like:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>My Joke Website</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background-color: white;
    }
    h1 {
      color: navy;
    }
    button {
      color: blue;
      font-weight: bold;
      font-size: 16px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
  <div>
    <p>Funny Joke: </p>
    <button id="reveal">Push to Reveal Punchline</button>
    <p id="punchline">Punchline: </p>
  </div>

  <script>
    const button = document.getElementById("reveal");
    const punchline = document.getElementById("punchline");

    button.addEventListener("click", function() {
      punchline.textContent = "Punchline: Your joke here";
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```
This code creates a basic website layout with a heading, a joke, and a button. When the button is clicked, it will reveal the punchline, which can be customized to display the actual joke.
